4142       data Enrollment;
4143       format Class Class.;
4144       input Class _TOTAL_;
4145       datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.ENROLLMENT has 4 observations and 2 variables.

4150       ;
4151       proc format;
4152       value Design 1='A' 2='B' 3='C';
NOTE: Format DESIGN has been output.
4153       value Rating
4154       1='dislike very much'
4155       2='dislike'
4156       3='neutral'
4157       4='like'
4158       5='like very much';
NOTE: Format RATING has been output.
4159       run;


4160       data WebSurvey;
4161       format Class Class. Design Design. Rating Rating.;
4162       do Class=1 to 4;
4163       do Design=1 to 3;
4164       do Rating=1 to 5;
4165       input Count @@;
4166       output;
4167       end;
4168       end;
4169       end;
4170       datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.WEBSURVEY has 60 observations and 4 variables.

4175       ;
4176       data WebSurvey;
4177       set WebSurvey;
4178       if Class=1 then Weight=3734/300;
4179       if Class=2 then Weight=3565/300;
4180       if Class=3 then Weight=3903/300;
4181       if Class=4 then Weight=4196/300;
4182       run;

NOTE: There were 60 observations read from the data set WORK.WEBSURVEY.
NOTE: The data set WORK.WEBSURVEY has 60 observations and 5 variables.

4183       proc surveylogistic data=WebSurvey total=Enrollment;
4184       stratum Class;
4185       freq Count;
4186       class Design;
4187       model Rating (order=internal) = design;
4188       weight Weight;
4189       run;

NOTE: PROC SURVEYLOGISTIC is fitting the cumulative logit model. The probabilities modeled are summed over the responses having the lower Ordered Values in the 
      Response Profile table.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE SURVEYLOGISTIC printed page 245.

4190       proc surveylogistic data=WebSurvey total=Enrollment;
4191       stratum Class;
4192       freq Count;
4193       class Design;
4194       model Rating (ref='neutral') = Design /link=glogit;
4195       weight Weight;
4196       run;

NOTE: PROC SURVEYLOGISTIC is fitting the generalized logit model. The logits modeled contrast each response category against the reference category 
      (Rating='neutral').
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE SURVEYLOGISTIC printed page 246.

